    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen a count is typed before a register prefix, the commands that Normal mode translates into operator commands (x, X, D, C, s, S, `<Del>`) apply the count twice, i.e. the count is squared. For example, `2\"_x` deletes 4 characters instead of 2, and `2\"_D` deletes 4 lines instead of 2.\n\nIt happens with any register (`2\"ax` too), not only the black hole register.\nNot affected:\n- count after the register: `\"_2x` deletes 2 characters,\n- the commands these translate to: `2\"_dl` deletes 2 characters,\n- Visual mode: `vl2\"_x`.\n\nPossibly a regression from 2514256d95 \"refactor(input): exec stuffed keys eagerly\". nv_optrans() now runs the stuffed translation (e.g. \"2dl\") at once via exec_stuffed(), before `cap->opcount = 0` runs, so it looks like the count that nv_regname() saved before '\"' is multiplied in again. I have not bisected this.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\nnvim --clean\n:call setline(1, 'abcdefgh')\n2\"_x\n```\nLine becomes \"efgh\".\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`2\"_x` deletes 2 characters, the same as `\"_2x` and `2\"_dl`, so the line becomes \"cdefgh\".\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev+1915-c5641b2bfb\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, vim 9.2.1202 gives \"cdefgh\"\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora Linux 44, kernel 7.2.11-200.fc44.x86_64\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nKonsole, but not terminal specific\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nCopr repo for neovim-nightly owned by agriffis",
